26","LinkProvider":{"Name":"Europe PMC"},"RelationshipType":{"Name":"IsReferencedBy"},"Source":{"Type":{"Name":"literature"},"Identifier":{"ID":"30093494","IDScheme":"PMID"}},"Target":{"Type":{"Name":"dataset"},"Identifier":{"ID":"NF020893","IDScheme":"InterPro","IDURL":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/entry/NF020893"},"Title":"['This is the VTT (VMP1, TMEM41, and TVP38) domain found in sequences from all cellular organisms, including Golgi apparatus membrane protein TVP38 from Saccharomyces cerevisiae, which is involved in vesicular trafficking and spindle migration [1,2]. This domain was previously called SNARE-associated domain but was renamed as there is no evidence that it associates with SNARE proteins ([PMID:30093494]). (from Pfam)']","Publisher":{"Name":"InterPro"}}},{"ObtainedBy":"submission","PublicationDate":"11-02-2026","LinkProvider":{"Name":"Europe PMC"},"RelationshipType":{"Name":"IsReferencedBy"},"Source":{"Type":{"Name":"literature"},"Identifier":{"ID":"30093494","IDScheme":"PMID"}},"Target":{"Type":{"Name":"dataset"},"Identifier":{"ID":"IPR032816","IDScheme":"InterPro","IDURL":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/entry/IPR032816"},"Title":"['This entry represents a domain found in Golgi apparatus membrane protein TVP38 from Saccharomyces cerevisiae, in human Vacuole membrane protein 1 (VMP1) and Transmembrane protein 41B (TMEM41B). TVP38 localises with the t-SNARE Tlg2 [[PMID:16107716]] and is involved in vesicular trafficking and spindle migration [[PMID:17178117]]. VMP1 and TMEM41B are phospholipid scramblases involved in lipid homeostasis and membrane dynamics processes [[PMID:33929485], [PMID:33850023], [PMID:34015269], [PMID:","Publisher":{"Name":"InterPro"}}},{"ObtainedBy":"submission","PublicationDate":"11-02-2026","LinkProvider":{"Name":"Europe PMC"},"RelationshipType":{"Name":"IsReferencedBy"},"Source":{"Type":{"Name":"literature"},"Identifier":{"ID":"30093494","IDScheme":"PMID"}},"Target":{"Type":{"Name":"dataset"},"Identifier":{"ID":"PF09335","IDScheme":"InterPro","IDURL":"http://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/entry/PF09335"},"Title":"['This is the VTT (VMP1, TMEM41, and TVP38) domain found in sequences from all cellular organisms, including Golgi apparatus membrane protein TVP38 from Saccharomyces cerevisiae, which is involved in vesicular trafficking and spindle migration [[PMID:16107716],[PMID:17178117]]. This domain was previously called SNARE-associated domain but was renamed as there is no evidence that it associates with SNARE proteins [[PMID:30093494]].']","Publisher":{"Name":"InterPro"}}}]}}]}]}}